; error: 12:7: 'f' changes what its first value reaches, so it can't be given what fixed 'xs' owns; give it a copy, 'xs.copy() at r', or keep 'xs' in a flex variable
; A call through a task value whose type says 'flex' is checked as a call of a
; task with a flex parameter: what a fixed name owns can't be given there.

task zero(flex xs: [int]@r)
    xs[0] = 0
fi
task main()
    region r default
    fixed xs = [1, 2, ...]
    fixed f: (flex [int]@r) -> nothing = zero
    f(xs)
fi
